{
  "_comment": [
    "Spell slots granted per class, indexed by that class's OWN level (see",
    "characterClassLevel() in class-features.js for the same idea applied to",
    "features) — not the character's total level. `slotsByLevel` maps a level",
    "(as a string key, '1'..'20') to an array of nine numbers: how many slots",
    "of spell level 1 through 9 a character of that class level has. A class",
    "not listed here grants no spell slots at all — read through",
    "spellSlotsForClass() in src/js/spells.js, never off this file directly.",
    "Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, and Wizard share the standard 5e full-caster",
    "progression; Paladin and Ranger share the standard half-caster progression",
    "(no slots at level 1, capped at 5th-level spells); Warlock uses the",
    "smaller, single-level Pact Magic table. Barbarian, Fighter, Monk, and",
    "Rogue grant no slots here — Fighter's Eldritch Knight and Rogue's Arcane",
    "Trickster are subclass-only third-casters, and this table is keyed by",
    "class name, not subclass, so listing Fighter/Rogue here would wrongly",
    "grant slots to every Fighter/Rogue.",
    "",
    "`multiclassSlotsByLevel` is the rules' own Multiclass Spellcaster table —",
    "same nine-number shape, but indexed by a character's blended MULTICLASS",
    "CASTER LEVEL, not any one class's own level: full-caster levels count in",
    "full, half-caster levels (Paladin, Ranger, Artificer) count floored by 2,",
    "and Eldritch Knight/Arcane Trickster levels count floored by 3, each",
    "class's contribution floored BEFORE summing (see multiclassCasterLevel()",
    "in src/js/spells.js). Numerically identical to the full-caster table above",
    "— that identity is the rules' own shorthand, not a coincidence here.",
    "Warlock's Pact Magic is never blended in; it stays its own pool, read off",
    "the Warlock entry above at the Warlock's own level."
  ],
